<metadata><name>Newport Unlimited 2026 distance race</name><desc>Newport Unlimited 2026 (NAASA / NEMA, Aug 15-16, 2026) distance race standard courses. Source: SI Appendix A - Distance Race (v1.0 final; the posted v1.1 file is the main SI, which refers to this appendix) and Sailing Instructions v1.1. Start: same line as the buoy races, rendezvous immediately S of Gould Island (approximate point). First mark for every course: RG EP Bell approx 0.4 NM NNE of the Newport Bridge centre span, left to port unless the course designation carries a lower-case s prefix (then starboard). Finish: line between an RC vessel and RG EP Bell. All marks to port except where noted (RG PI nun to starboard on DH). Any course may be signalled in reverse with -R (marks on the opposite side) - not drawn. Islands named as marks (Hope, Conanicut) are left to port; they are drawn with (routing) points, which are not marks. Cautions: shallow area 0.3 NM SSW of Hope Island; S of Dyer Island is shallow well beyond visible land. Newport Bridge only via the three centre spans, Jamestown Bridge only via the centre span (other bridge sections are obstructions); keep clear of the Navy security zone (do not pass E of the line from 200 yd W of the Coddington Cove breakwater light through R14 bell to the red-green can off Coasters Harbor Island). Windward/leeward buoy courses are not included.</desc></metadata>
